   "recovery": "Dublin carried 36.4 million passengers in 2025, 11.4% above 2019. It went past 2019 in 2023 (+1.8%). January to June 2026 was 17.9 million, 16.2% above the same months of 2019 and 5.8% above 2025.",
   "season": "In 2025 the busiest month (Aug, 3.78 million) had 1.77 times the traffic of the quietest (Feb, 2.14 million). In 2019 the same gap was 1.72 times (Jul vs Feb).",
   "growth": "Turkiye grew fastest (+69.8%). The UK added the most passengers (2.35 million) and the US added 1.06 million. Only 2 of 28 markets shrank: Lithuania (-8.9%), Bulgaria (-7.0%).",
   "share": "Dublin had 85.9% of passengers at the five main airports in 2019 and 83.7% in 2025. Its share was 72.8% in 2005. Cork rose from 6.8% to 8.0% and Shannon from 4.2% to 5.2% since 2019.",
   "concentration": "The top 10 country markets carried 79.0% of Dublin passengers in 2025 (80.9% in 2022). The UK alone is 27.8%. Data is by country, not by route."
